    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0285" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg205"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hill to Mr. Choate.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-01-07"><hi rendition="#italic">January 7,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 526.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In view of representations made to the
                    Department by the American Presbyterian Kongo Mission of their need of having
                    some one whom they can consult in matters arising between the mission and the
                    Government of the Kongo Free State, it is desired to have you make known to the
                    British Government the gratification which this Government would experience in
                    learning that the British consul at Boma had been authorized to take care of
                    American interests in the Kongo Free State until United States consular
                    representation there is provided for by Congressional action.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">David J. Hill</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
